course: dictionary
lesson: 12504
title: Depleted: running low
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Depleted means reduced, so that not much is left, because it has been used up. «The camp's water supplies were depleted by the end of the hot week.» The clue is "by the end of the hot week": the water was used bit by bit until very little was left.
explain: Depleted comes from the verb deplete, which means to use up or empty out. Check your meaning by swapping in "used up": «The depleted shelves» means shelves with only a few things left on them. Depleted can also describe a team with many players missing, usually because of injuries.
explain: In science, depleted can mean that part of something has been taken away. «Depleted soil» has lost some of the goodness plants need to grow. «The ozone layer is depleted» is a warning that something protecting the Earth has been worn thin, so people must look after nature.
fact: Depleted means reduced in amount, so that not much is left.
fact: «Depleted» is the past form of the verb deplete, which means to use up or empty out.
fact: In sport, a depleted team is weakened because many of its players are missing.
fact: In science, «depleted soil» and «ozone-depleted» mean that part of something has been removed or worn away.
fact: Phrases like «depleted stocks», «depleted supplies» and «badly depleted» show how much has been lost.
exercise: «The farmer's depleted soil gave poor crops.» What does depleted soil mean? | Soil that is brand new | Soil that is wet and muddy | *Soil with much of its goodness used up | Soil that is full of stones
exercise: «Our team was depleted by injuries, so we had only nine players.» What does depleted mean here? | Very tired after running | Full of new players | Happy and excited | *Weakened because many players were missing
exercise: Dad says his phone battery is depleted. What does he mean? | It has a big, shiny screen | It is loud and fast | *It has very little charge left | It is brand new
test: «The shop's supplies of bread were depleted by lunchtime.» Which word is closest in meaning to depleted? | Full | Hidden | *Used up | Delivered
test: Which sentence shows depleted fish stocks? | The fish are bigger than ever | Fish are swimming in the sea in large numbers | *Too many fish have been caught, so very few are left | The sea is warm and calm
exam: Why does «depleted soil» matter for farmers? | It makes the soil lighter | *Plants cannot grow well in it | It stops the rain falling | It makes the farm bigger
